    {
      "id": "claim_2a547a204bd34f7e84b0b4a852222e6f",
      "statement": "Curation failure semantics distinguish infrastructure failures from row failures: transient Postgres SQLSTATE classes (08, 40, 53, 57) and client-side connection codes abort the pass leaving rows recoverable; an unreachable object store (RawReadError) aborts rather than deferring; a genuinely absent object defers to deferred_missing_raw; a row-specific failure parks the observation on terminal curation_failed (outside RECOVERABLE_STATUSES so it is never re-selected), and after MAX_PARKED_PER_PASS (5) parked rows the pass throws TooManyParkedObservationsError in case the failure is systemic.",
      "evidence": [
